    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0667" n="582" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.61383/172: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-14T15:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">November 14,
                                1919, 3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            November 15, 10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3275. Mrs. Jenkins has just telegraphed that her husband was imprisoned in Puebla
                    today. Jenkins and Mestre<anchor n="59" xml:id="d547-f1"/> report that evidence
                    on which arrest was made is false and was extracted from persons testifying by
                    threats of death.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d547-f1" n="59" xml:id="d547-f1-content">
                <p>Attorney for Mr. Jenkins.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
